<SiteLayout title="About Retail POS Mobile" description="About the goals, development stage, and product principles behind Retail POS Mobile." path="/about/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><span class="eyebrow">About the project</span><h1>Built around the work a shop does every day.</h1><p>Retail POS Mobile is an independent Android-first retail POS project. It is currently establishing its foundation before public business workflows are released.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container content-wrap"><h2>Why build it carefully?</h2><p>Point-of-sale software touches sales, stock, and cash records. A polished homepage cannot substitute for correct transaction behavior, durable storage, safe retries, and clear recovery paths. Those foundations need to come before claims about reliability.</p><h2>Who is it intended for?</h2><p>The product is being shaped around small retail operations, including general-store workflows and Pakistan's PKR context. Exact support for payments, units, reports, devices, and other workflows will be documented after implementation and testing.</p><h2>How we will communicate progress</h2><ul><li>Planned work stays labelled as planned.</li><li>Release notes describe only approved, published builds.</li><li>Download information includes version, build, compatibility, and checksum details.</li><li>Known limitations are documented rather than hidden behind broad claims.</li></ul><p><a class="text-link" href="/changelog/">Follow the release history <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></div></section></SiteLayout>
